/////////////////////////////////////////
// V-Ray for Blender - node thumbnail scene
//
// GENERATED, do not hand-edit: exported from a V-Ray render of Blender's own material-preview
// scene (preferences: export_material_preview_scene, with compression and hex off) and then
// renamed by _split_test/buildscene.py. Regenerate it the same way if the preview scene
// changes. Keeping it a verbatim copy is the point - it is what makes a BRDF/material node
// thumbnail match the Preview panel.
//
// Loaded server-side into a warm preview renderer. A thumbnail request only re-exports the
// previewed node's material plugins, repoints the subject's 'material' and toggles 'visible',
// so this scene is set up once per renderer rather than per thumbnail.
//
// Contract with the client (preview/thumbs/render.py):
//   thumbNode         - Blender's preview sphere; wears the material for the BRDF/material tier
//   thumbPlaneNode    - the flat swatch; wears the material for the flat texture tier
//   thumbBackdropNode - Blender's preview floor, shown with the sphere only
//   thumbMtl          - placeholder material, replaced at runtime
//   thumbCamera       - RenderView/SettingsCamera scene_name, must match vray.setCameraName()
//
// Do not hand-edit light colours into the raw 'color' attribute form: 'color' is ACOLOR, and a
// 3-float list there is read as black.
/////////////////////////////////////////

SettingsPhotonMap settingsPhotonMap {
  bounces=10;
  max_photons=30;
